  "hypothesis": "The archived H20 case is not transportable to a different memory system, so this is a separate pre-registration on the AutoDL RTX 6000D host. The claim is unchanged: an MLP block at 4096 tokens with hidden 7168 keeps its gate and up projections in one [4096, 14336] bf16 buffer, and the shipped F.silu(x[:, :7168]) * x[:, 7168:] launches two kernels and round-trips a 58.7 MB silu intermediate. A single fused pass that reads the 117.4 MB buffer once and writes 58.7 MB is expected to recover most of the gap to a kernel that moves the same bytes.\n",
  "mechanism": {
    "name": "one fused silu_and_mul pass over the interleaved gate/up buffer",
    "class": "fusion",
    "justification": "torch.add(a, b) moves exactly the fused kernel's bytes with the same contiguous access pattern and finishes in 0.10834 ms, so the missing time is addressable, not a property of the workload. The fused Triton kernel is bit-identical to the shipped path, so the output distribution is unchanged.\n"
